title: ApacheCon Europe 2000
template: page-event-landing
ref: apachecon-eu-2000

ApacheCon Europe 2000 was the first ApacheCon held in Europe, organized by the [[]Apache Software Foundation](http://www.apache.org/) and held 23–25 October 2000 at the Olympia Conference Centre in London, England. Over three days of sessions, keynotes, and an exhibition, it brought the Apache developer community together with users and vendors from across Europe and beyond.

## Keynotes

- **KN01 — Sun and Apache**, presented by George Paolini (Sun Microsystems), on the Java Community Process and Sun's involvement with Apache projects.
- **KN02 — IBM and Open Source: A Software Agenda**, presented by Kristof Kloeckner (IBM).
- **KN03 — Living In a Virtual World**, a keynote by **Douglas Adams**, author of *The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy* — his personal view of the promise, achievements, and absurdities of information and digital technology.
- **KN04 — Convincing Management to Let You Work on Open Development.**
- **KN05 — Perspectives on the Jakarta Project.**

## Sessions

The programme ran across the Auditorium and three classrooms, with tracks spanning Apache 2.0 internals and module development, PHP, mod_perl, Tomcat and Java servlets, XML and Cocoon, security and SSL, and real-world web hosting. Monday through Wednesday featured more than forty sessions plus Birds of a Feather gatherings each evening. See the full [[]session schedule](sessions) and the surviving [[]presentation materials](presentations).

## Exhibition

The expo floor featured exhibitors including IBM, Sun Microsystems, Oracle, Covalent Technologies, Collab.Net, Fujitsu Siemens Computers, O'Reilly Network, BSDi, and others.

